od so do please  check on those and and obviously don't  forget to put the bins out myself and  the deputy leader of the council also  spent a shift a day shift each with some  of the refuse collection teams and it  was a really fantastic experience it  absolutely poured it down with rain on  my shift where I I did some bins in  drumfield lunston and cutthorpe  unfortunately for cancer Cupid she had a  fairly dry day I wasn't so lucky but it  was a really fantastic experience it was  great to walk a mile in in the shoes of  art or several miles if you like in the  shoes of our refuse collectors and  really really understand a bit more  about what they have to do and it made  me really really grateful and  appreciative for the work that they do  day in day out to do something as simple  as keeping our bins emptied and what a  mess we would be in without them so I  want to say a really big thank you to  all of our refuse teams and all of our  street scene Services who do some  fantastic work to keep the districts  looking clean and tidy you know and it's  great to be able to show a bit of  appreciation for them and and and  demonstrate really how what they have to  go through on a on a daily basis so well  done to them and a particular thank you  to the teams that looked at looked after  Charlotte and myself during the recent  the recent outings we'll be back out  again and actually in a couple of weeks  time I'll be I'll be spending some time  with some of our Leisure Center staff as  well to understand a bit more about  their work and how they how they're  getting on and we're doing a range of  these back to the floor sessions over  the coming weeks to just really get get  to grips with what our staff are having  to do in terms of some of the services  that we deliver so you'll be finding  more out about that in future briefings  I'm sure as I've mentioned in previous  leaders briefings we're taking a lot of  tough action on issues like flight  tipping and littering and we're really  trying to get to grips with some of the  issues that that residents across the  districts are experiencing and really  trying to make sure that we clean and  tidy up our beautiful countryside  surroundings and so a few of the things  that we've been doing we've had some  high profile prosecutions we've seized  and crushed the vehicle and issued some  pretty hefty fines we've also increased  the the the fines that we distribute to  the maximum possible allow amount that  we're allowed to set them at and we're  also doing things like deploying CCTV in  hiding CCTV and known fly tipping  Hospital spots to try and catch the  perpetrators while they're in the act  and we quite recently had a prosecution  successful prosecution of 300 pounds to  a waste collector who failed to provide  the necessary documentation for  collecting and disposing of waste and  this is a really useful reminder  hopefully that serves to all businesses  and all residents that if you pay  someone to collect your waste you must  check that they have the proper  documentation or else actually you could  be liable yourself so really do check  check into that and look into that and  be really careful about that and  obviously you know I hope you'll support  us in our efforts to really crack down  and get really really tough on fly  tipping and littering we can't allow it  to Scourge our communities in the way  that it has done in the past  now recently myself and the chair of the  council councilor Diana Ruff as well as  a senior officer went to an event an  armed forces event at the National  Memorial Arboretum to collect our Gold  Award now you may have heard about this  in previous editions but we won this we  wanted only 550 Employers in the whole  country out of about 7 million to have  been awarded the Gold Award as part of  the Armed Forces Covenant and this is  really about all the work that we do to  support the Armed Forces community and  reservists who work for the council so  really really pleased and really proud  of the council to be able to go and  collect that award and a big thank you  as well to our Armed Forces Champion  councilor Martin Thacker for all the  work he's done in in driving it forward  as well but it was great to be able to  go there and to receive that award along  with a few other councils in the area  which was really pleasing to see and  lots of other employers so great award  great event to be at and thank you very  much to the Armed Forces Community for  all of their support in terms of our  application you might also be aware that  the chair of the council councilor Diana  roof has a chair's appeal this year as  we always do and Diana's charity of  choice this time is safer the Armed  Forces charity now Dan is also hosting a  70s themed Disco Night at uh sherland on  the 2nd of December she's selling  tickets on our website so if you are  able to to join her for that event and  help contribute to a really valuable and  worthy cause please do go along please  go on our website and have a look about  how you can secure your tickets as I say  it'll be a fantastic night lots of great  tunes on and a good opportunity to to  contribute to this fantastic cause as  well now obviously following the very  sad passing of her majesty Queen  Elizabeth the Queen's green canopy  scheme has continued it was King  Charles's uh view that the schemats  continue and we're really we're really  pleased to be invited along with all the  other districts and Borough councils to  plant I think it was eight trees uh  Country Park is a special sort of cops  in memory of the queen and it was great  to be there to see some local  organizations honored as part of that as  well landmarks College based in  eckington was one of the recipients of  one of the trees and got to got to be  there as part of the tree planting as  well as well as a range of other  organizations and it was great to be  there and great to be part of a really  fantastic event to help honor the queen  and also to plant more trees it's a big  Derbyshire ambition at the minute to try  and plant a million trees over the next  few years so this is going some small  way to helping achieve that and for a  really good cause in memory of our  fantastic at Lake Majesty Queen  Elizabeth II so thanks very much for  watching this latest leaders briefing I  hope you found it useful and and you  picked up some useful information there  as I said at the very beginning please  do go on our website for more  information particularly around the cost  of living but also in relation to all  the other things that I've covered in  the briefing there's lots of information  on the website and please do follow  followers on our social media channels  Facebook Twitter and the like and I look  forward to seeing you next month where  we'll be talking a bit more about  Christmas thanks very much
 

